From: CarrotPilot <ajouatom@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: pd: accept capability mismatch current requests

USB PD sinks may set Capability Mismatch and place their desired maximum
current above the selected source PDO in the RDO.  The actual operating
current must remain within the advertised source limit, but the desired
maximum is allowed to exceed it when Capability Mismatch is set.

The existing Qualcomm policy engine rejects both fields unconditionally.
That causes hubs requesting 1.5 A operating / 3 A desired maximum from the
1.5 A comma source to loop on Reject with RDO 0x1702592c.

Match the validation used by the upstream Linux TCPM policy engine.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/pd/policy_engine.c b/drivers/usb/pd/policy_engine.c
index 6685f05..6f1774b 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/pd/policy_engine.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/pd/policy_engine.c
@@ -1196,11 +1196,18 @@ static void usbpd_set_state(struct usbpd *pd, enum usbpd_state next_state)
 		break;
 
 	case PE_SRC_NEGOTIATE_CAPABILITY:
+		/*
+		 * A sink that cannot be fully satisfied may set Capability Mismatch
+		 * and report its desired maximum current above the selected source
+		 * PDO.  Accept that standards-compliant request as long as the actual
+		 * operating current stays within our advertised 1.5 A limit.
+		 */
 		if (PD_RDO_OBJ_POS(pd->rdo) != 1 ||
 			PD_RDO_FIXED_CURR(pd->rdo) >
 				PD_SRC_PDO_FIXED_MAX_CURR(*default_src_caps) ||
-			PD_RDO_FIXED_CURR_MINMAX(pd->rdo) >
-				PD_SRC_PDO_FIXED_MAX_CURR(*default_src_caps)) {
+			(PD_RDO_FIXED_CURR_MINMAX(pd->rdo) >
+				PD_SRC_PDO_FIXED_MAX_CURR(*default_src_caps) &&
+			 !PD_RDO_MISMATCH(pd->rdo))) {
 			/* send Reject */
 			ret = pd_send_msg(pd, MSG_REJECT, NULL, 0, SOP_MSG);
 			if (ret) {
